name issue_84_quality_scaling_720p_low_rate
describe 720p camera on a 400 kbps link with libwebrtc's quality scaling: the initial frame drop scales it down before the first frame, and the QP then stays inside the H.264 thresholds
duration 30s
quality_scaling on
at 0s capacity=400kbps delay=30ms queue=300ms
# Issue #84 step 4: QualityScalerResource with MAINTAIN_FRAMERATE and
# VideoStreamEncoder::DropDueToSize (rtp::VideoSendController, `quality_scaling`).
# The video target at the start is under 300 kbps, so 720p is dropped as too
# large and the resolution steps down 3/5 at a time (VideoStreamAdapter)
# through VideoAdapter's series 960x540, 640x360, 480x270, 320x180: four
# dropped frames, then 320x180 for the call. Without quality scaling the same
# link encodes 720p at QP > 37 (issue_84_encoder_qp_720p_low_rate).
expect video.encode_height_mean < 360
expect video.qp_mean <= 37
expect video.render_fps > 25
